      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added these as #ifndef rules similar to gen_syscalls-inl.h. The syscall numbers we care about for landlock (444, 445, and 446) seem to be the same across x86_64, i386, and arm64 (https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/third_party/qemu/linux-headers/asm-x86/unistd_64.h;l\u003d361, https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/third_party/appliance_linux/packages/linux/linux_5_17/arch/arm/tools/syscall.tbl;l\u003d462, https://source.corp.google.com/piper///depot/google3/third_party/appliance_linux/packages/linux/linux_5_17/arch/arm64/include/asm/unistd32.h;l\u003d902?q\u003dlandlock\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2FPiper:google3%2Fthird_party%2Fappliance_linux%2Fpackages%2Flinux%2Flinux_5_17%2Farch%2Farm64%2F).\n\nBased on our GVC discussion, it also sounds like the kernel version will not always match the header version on ChromeOS.",
